#question(title: [More on the definition of maximum], centered: true)[
  Let $f$ be a function with domain $I$.  \
  What does each of the following mean?

  + $display(exists C in RR)$ s.t.
    $display(forall x in I)$,
    $display(f(x) <= C)$
  + $display(exists C in RR)$ s.t.
    $display(forall x in I)$,
    $display(f(x) < C)$
  + $display(exists a in I)$ s.t.
    $display(forall x in I)$,
    $display(f(x) <= f(a))$
  + $display(exists a in I)$ s.t.
    $display(forall x in I)$,
    $display(f(x) < f(a))$
]
